<title>UK: ROWING-CAMBRIDGE WIN UNIVERSITY BOAT RACE AGAIN.</title>
<headline>ROWING-CAMBRIDGE WIN UNIVERSITY BOAT RACE AGAIN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cambridge won the 143rd University Boat Race on Saturday, beating Oxford by six seconds in one of the closest races for many years.</p>
<p>Cambridge covered the 4 miles 374 yards (7-km)  River Thames course from Putney to Mortlake in 17 minutes 38 seconds to record their fifth successive victory and their 74th in all.</p>
